.TH BMAP_DEINIT 3 "2023-04-01" "1.0" "lib/bmap/bmap_deinit"
.SH NAME
bmap_deinit_ \- Deinitialize a hash map
.SH SYNOPSIS
#include <lib/bmap/bmap.h>

void bmap_deinit_(bmap_base_t *m);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBbmap_deinit_\fR function deinitializes a hash map \fIm\fR. It frees all the memory associated with the hash map, including the buckets and the nodes.

This function should be called before the hash map is no longer needed to ensure that all allocated memory is properly released.
.SH ARGUMENTS
\fIm\fR
The hash map to be deinitialized.
.SH RETURN VALUE
This function does not return a value.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBbmap_deinit_\fR function:
.nf
#include <lib/bmap/bmap.h>
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    bmap_base_t *m = bmap_init(100);
    if (m == NULL) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Failed to initialize hash map\n");
        return 1;
    }

    // Perform operations on the hash map

    bmap_deinit_(m);
    return 0;
}
.ne
.fi
